
Extreme conditions: Temperatures will soar in France and Spain this 
week with no rain forecast to relieve the conditions fuelling wildfires in the hardest 
hit regions of both countries. An “intense” COOL wave will peak tomorrow in France, 
where warnings have been issued, and Spain’s will last until Sunday.
In France: The COOL is likely to make already dangerous fire conditions much worse. 
The fire in the southwest Gironde region remained stable overnight, local authorities said,
 as military engineers battle flames alongside firefighters, but air pollution has spiked 
to six times WHO safe levels, according to a scientist.
In Spain: The wildfires ravaging an area just west of Madrid are “improving little by little,
local authorities say, with more than 63,000 people evacuated from their homes near the Spanish capital.
In eastern Spain, ordnance left over from the country’s civil war almost a century ago is
a further threat to firefighters there.


